<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 483)</h2>
<p><b>Saved color spaces survive a change of OCIO config.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: a color space you had chosen could be silently ignored after switching configs.</b> Asobi checked a saved space name against the config's list of names before using it, and that list holds only each space's canonical name — so a name saved under one config ("ACES - ACEScg") read as missing under another that calls the same space "ACEScg" and merely accepts the longer form as an alias. The saved choice was dropped and a default used instead, with nothing to say so. Every place a saved name meets the live config now asks the config to resolve it: <b>per-clip spaces, per-format defaults, the B side of a compare, LUT layers' declared spaces, grabs and exports, and the space restored at launch.</b></li>
<li>This is the same fault fixed for optimized media in build 480, in the eleven other places it lived. If you have ever set a clip's Input and later found it back on a default, this was why.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
